<title>USA: U.S. 30-year bond auction average 6.619 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 30-year bond auction average 6.619 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its auction of 30-year bonds produced these results:</p>
<p>			 30-YEAR BONDS DUE NOV 15, 2026</p>
<p>			     $10.000 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> LOW	 6.618    Awarded At	98.470	6-1/2</p>
<p> HIGH	6.625    High Yield	98.380     Percent</p>
<p> AVERAGE   6.619    51 Percent	98.457</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.68 Times</p>
<p>	   Tail -- (High Minus Average Yield) =  1   Basis Pts</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 15.Nov.26</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    30-YEAR BONDS		  PAY DATE 15.Nov.96</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 07.Nov.96</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  10.000 BLN USD		 CUSIP    912810EY0</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   26.841			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   258.00 MLN			AUCTION AVERAGES</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.500</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN  0.00 MLN			 PRICE	 98.457</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    6.625-6.618 PCT		YIELD	  6.619</p>
<p> AVERAGE YIELD DOWN FROM 6.768 PCT AT AUCTION ON 08.AUG.96</p>
<p> AVG YIELD LOWEST SINCE 6.119 PCT AT AUCTION ON 08.FEB.96</p>
